==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*mek}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*me}}. The word is inflected as plural, but there is no plural marker in the nominative, except in dialects ({{m-lite|fi|met}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Pronoun===
{{head-lite|fi|pronouns|cat2=personal pronouns}}

# [[we]]
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|fi|'''Me''' emme unohda.|'''We''' will not forget.}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|fi|Näin '''meidän''' kesken...|Just between '''us'''...}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|fi|Mennäänkö '''meille'''?|Should we go over '''to our place'''?}}

====Usage notes====
* Although usually omitted in written language (the verb shows both the person and the number), the pronoun is in spoken language used very often (compare the usage of {{m-lite|fi|minä||I}}).

====Inflection====
* Irregular (inflectional stem {{m-lite|fi||mei-}}, as if in the plural). The [[comitative]] and [[instructive]] forms don't exist; the [[abessive]] is hardly used.
* In addition to the standard set of cases, {{m-lite|fi|me}} and the other personal pronouns have a specific [[accusative]] form, {{m-lite|fi|meidät}}.
